1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,572
Welcome to Algebra One. Before we solve a
single equation, we need to know what

2
00:00:04,572 --> 00:00:06,656
kinds of numbers we're working with.

3
00:00:07,106 --> 00:00:11,442
In this lesson, we'll sort numbers into
families, and see where every one of them

4
00:00:11,442 --> 00:00:12,781
lives on the number line.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,539
Let's start with the numbers you first
learned: one, two, three, and so on.

6
00:00:18,989 --> 00:00:22,274
These are the natural numbers, also called
counting numbers.

7
00:00:22,724 --> 00:00:25,540
Add zero to that list, and you get the
whole numbers.

8
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:31,189
Now include the negatives: negative one,
negative two, negative three.

9
00:00:31,639 --> 00:00:34,306
Together with the whole numbers, they make
the integers.

10
00:00:34,756 --> 00:00:39,880
On the number line, integers sit at evenly
spaced marks, stretching forever in both

11
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:40,559
directions.

12
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:46,137
But there are numbers between the marks,
like one half, or negative three fourths.

13
00:00:46,587 --> 00:00:51,145
Any number that can be written as a
fraction, one integer over another,

14
00:00:51,145 --> 00:00:53,649
non-zero integer, is a rational number.

15
00:00:54,099 --> 00:00:59,112
Every integer is rational too, because
five, for example, equals five over one.

16
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:02,815
Rational numbers also show up as decimals.

17
00:01:03,265 --> 00:01:08,107
Their decimals either stop, like zero
point seven five, which is three fourths,

18
00:01:08,557 --> 00:01:13,759
or repeat forever in a pattern, like zero
point three three three, and so on, which

19
00:01:13,759 --> 00:01:14,573
is one third.

20
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,946
Some numbers can't be written as a
fraction at all. Their decimals go on

21
00:01:19,946 --> 00:01:21,951
forever with no repeating pattern.

22
00:01:22,401 --> 00:01:26,518
These are irrational numbers. The square
root of two is one. So is pi.

23
00:01:26,968 --> 00:01:32,215
They still have exact spots on the number
line. The square root of two is about one

24
00:01:32,215 --> 00:01:35,565
point four one, and pi is about three
point one four.

25
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:41,137
Put the rational and irrational numbers
together, and you get the real numbers.

26
00:01:41,587 --> 00:01:46,345
Here's the whole family. Natural numbers
sit inside the whole numbers, which sit

27
00:01:46,345 --> 00:01:49,438
inside the integers, which sit inside the
rationals.

28
00:01:49,888 --> 00:01:54,694
The irrationals sit beside the rationals,
and together they fill the entire number

29
00:01:54,694 --> 00:01:54,987
line.

30
00:01:56,133 --> 00:02:00,926
The number line also lets us compare
numbers. A number to the right is always

31
00:02:00,926 --> 00:02:01,424
greater.

32
00:02:01,874 --> 00:02:06,674
So negative two is greater than negative
five, even though five looks bigger.

33
00:02:07,124 --> 00:02:11,839
Negative two is to the right, so negative
two is greater than negative five.

34
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:18,183
Your turn. Classify each number: negative
four, the square root of nine, two thirds,

35
00:02:18,183 --> 00:02:19,921
and the square root of five.

36
00:02:20,371 --> 00:02:23,977
Pause the video, and decide which families
each one belongs to.

37
00:02:24,427 --> 00:02:28,181
Negative four is an integer, so it's also
rational and real.

38
00:02:28,631 --> 00:02:33,655
The square root of nine equals three, so
it's natural, whole, an integer, rational,

39
00:02:33,655 --> 00:02:34,199
and real.

40
00:02:34,649 --> 00:02:39,601
Two thirds is rational and real. And the
square root of five is irrational and

41
00:02:39,601 --> 00:02:39,919
real.

42
00:02:41,166 --> 00:02:44,046
Let's put the number line to work with a
worked example.

43
00:02:46,266 --> 00:02:51,030
Order these five numbers from least to
greatest: negative one point six, the

44
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:55,669
square root of three, negative five
thirds, zero point seven five, and two

45
00:02:55,669 --> 00:02:59,493
thirds. Then say which are rational and
which are irrational.

46
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:06,180
The trick is to write every number as a
decimal. Negative five thirds is negative

47
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,441
one point six six six, repeating.

48
00:03:09,566 --> 00:03:15,396
Negative one point six is negative one
point six zero zero. Since negative one

49
00:03:15,396 --> 00:03:20,403
point six six six is further left,
negative five thirds is smaller.

50
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:24,519
Two thirds is zero point six six six,
repeating.

51
00:03:25,666 --> 00:03:31,238
Zero point seven five is bigger than zero
point six six six, because seven tenths

52
00:03:31,238 --> 00:03:32,407
beats six tenths.

53
00:03:33,533 --> 00:03:38,695
The square root of three is between one
point seven and one point eight, about one

54
00:03:38,695 --> 00:03:41,277
point seven three two. It is the largest.

55
00:03:42,399 --> 00:03:46,984
So the order is negative five thirds,
negative one point six, two thirds, zero

56
00:03:46,984 --> 00:03:51,805
point seven five, and the square root of
three. Four of these are rational because

57
00:03:51,805 --> 00:03:56,331
they can be written as fractions. The
square root of three is irrational: its

58
00:03:56,331 --> 00:03:58,506
decimal never ends and never repeats.

59
00:03:59,633 --> 00:04:04,081
Watch out for three things. With
negatives, the number farther from zero is

60
00:04:04,081 --> 00:04:08,827
the smaller one. A repeating decimal is
still rational. And the square root of a

61
00:04:08,827 --> 00:04:11,793
number that is not a perfect square is
irrational.

62
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:17,988
Your turn. Order negative three fourths,
negative zero point eight, the square root

63
00:04:17,988 --> 00:04:21,338
of two, and one point four. Pause the
video and try it.

64
00:04:25,866 --> 00:04:30,818
Negative zero point eight is smallest,
then negative three fourths, which is

65
00:04:30,818 --> 00:04:36,031
negative zero point seven five. Then one
point four, and the square root of two,

66
00:04:36,031 --> 00:04:39,029
about one point four one four, is the
largest.

67
00:04:39,166 --> 00:04:40,166
Next up: Order of Operations. If this
helped, subscribe to School STEM,

68
00:04:40,166 --> 00:04:42,001
What is three plus four times two?

69
00:04:42,451 --> 00:04:47,229
If you said fourteen, you added first. If
you said eleven, you multiplied first.

70
00:04:47,679 --> 00:04:51,713
Only one of those can be right, and in
this lesson we'll learn the rule that

71
00:04:51,713 --> 00:04:52,138
decides.

72
00:04:53,266 --> 00:04:58,320
Mathematicians agree on an order of
operations, so that every expression has

73
00:04:58,320 --> 00:04:59,517
exactly one value.

74
00:04:59,967 --> 00:05:02,292
First, grouping symbols, like parentheses.

75
00:05:02,742 --> 00:05:03,937
Second, exponents.

76
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:08,035
Third, multiplication and division,
working from left to right.

77
00:05:08,485 --> 00:05:11,877
Fourth, addition and subtraction, also
from left to right.

78
00:05:12,999 --> 00:05:15,815
Back to our question. Three plus four
times two.

79
00:05:16,265 --> 00:05:20,319
Multiplication comes before addition, so
four times two is eight.

80
00:05:20,769 --> 00:05:23,905
Then three plus eight is eleven. The
answer is eleven.

81
00:05:25,499 --> 00:05:30,580
Multiplication and division are partners.
Neither one always goes first. You just

82
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,771
work left to right.

83
00:05:32,221 --> 00:05:37,064
In twelve divided by three, times two, we
divide first, because it's on the left.

84
00:05:37,514 --> 00:05:41,162
Twelve divided by three is four, and four
times two is eight.

85
00:05:42,299 --> 00:05:44,625
The same goes for addition and
subtraction.

86
00:05:45,075 --> 00:05:49,085
Ten minus four plus three: subtract first,
because it's on the left.

87
00:05:49,535 --> 00:05:53,482
Ten minus four is six, and six plus three
is nine. Not three!

88
00:05:54,599 --> 00:05:59,723
Let's try a longer one: two times, open
parenthesis, five minus three, close

89
00:05:59,723 --> 00:06:03,026
parenthesis, squared, plus eight divided
by four.

90
00:06:03,476 --> 00:06:06,143
Parentheses first: five minus three is
two.

91
00:06:06,593 --> 00:06:08,747
Exponents next: two squared is four.

92
00:06:09,197 --> 00:06:14,590
Now multiply and divide, left to right:
two times four is eight, and eight divided

93
00:06:14,590 --> 00:06:15,576
by four is two.

94
00:06:16,026 --> 00:06:18,031
Finally, add: eight plus two is ten.

95
00:06:18,166 --> 00:06:24,324
One more thing about exponents. Negative
three squared, with no parentheses, means

96
00:06:24,324 --> 00:06:27,721
the negative of three squared, which is
negative nine.

97
00:06:28,171 --> 00:06:32,705
But negative three in parentheses,
squared, means negative three times

98
00:06:32,705 --> 00:06:35,232
negative three, which is positive nine.

99
00:06:35,682 --> 00:06:38,327
Parentheses tell you exactly what gets
squared.

100
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:44,223
Your turn. Simplify: eighteen minus six
divided by three, plus two cubed.

101
00:06:44,673 --> 00:06:46,124
Pause the video and try it.

102
00:06:46,574 --> 00:06:48,579
Exponents first: two cubed is eight.

103
00:06:49,029 --> 00:06:51,739
Then division: six divided by three is
two.

104
00:06:52,189 --> 00:06:57,299
Now, left to right: eighteen minus two is
sixteen, and sixteen plus eight is twenty

105
00:06:57,299 --> 00:06:57,607
four.

106
00:06:58,733 --> 00:07:03,704
Now a worked example with every part of
the order of operations in one problem.

107
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:10,131
Evaluate eighteen divided by three
squared, times two, minus the quantity

108
00:07:10,131 --> 00:07:12,664
four minus seven, squared, plus five.

109
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:17,938
Start inside the parentheses. Four minus
seven is negative three.

110
00:07:19,066 --> 00:07:24,172
Next, exponents. Three squared is nine,
and negative three squared is positive

111
00:07:24,172 --> 00:07:27,706
nine, because a negative times a negative
is positive.

112
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:34,179
Now multiplication and division, from left
to right. Eighteen divided by nine comes

113
00:07:34,179 --> 00:07:35,468
first, which is two.

114
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,157
Then two times two is four.

115
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:44,877
Finally, addition and subtraction from
left to right. Four minus nine is negative

116
00:07:44,877 --> 00:07:47,769
five, and negative five plus five is zero.

117
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:53,636
The answer is zero. Notice how every step
did just one kind of operation.

118
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:59,117
Watch out. Multiplication and division
have the same rank, so you go left to

119
00:07:59,117 --> 00:08:03,467
right. The parentheses matter with
negatives: negative three in parentheses,

120
00:08:03,467 --> 00:08:07,818
squared, is nine, but negative three
squared without parentheses is negative

121
00:08:07,818 --> 00:08:11,940
nine. And writing one kind of operation
per line prevents most mistakes.

122
00:08:13,066 --> 00:08:18,287
Your turn. Evaluate forty minus two times
the quantity three plus one, squared,

123
00:08:18,287 --> 00:08:21,194
divided by four. Pause the video and try
it.

124
00:08:24,733 --> 00:08:31,163
Three plus one is four, and four squared
is sixteen. Two times sixteen is thirty

125
00:08:31,163 --> 00:08:35,440
two, divided by four is eight. Forty minus
eight is thirty two.

126
00:08:36,566 --> 00:08:41,323
Algebra starts with one simple idea: using
a letter to stand for a number.

127
00:08:41,773 --> 00:08:46,539
In this lesson, we'll learn what variables
and expressions are, and how to evaluate

128
00:08:46,539 --> 00:08:49,581
an expression when we know the value of
its variable.

129
00:08:50,699 --> 00:08:55,785
A variable is a letter, like x, n, or t,
that represents a number we don't know

130
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:57,910
yet, or a number that can change.

131
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:03,781
For example, if a movie ticket costs eight
dollars, then n tickets cost eight times n

132
00:09:03,781 --> 00:09:04,291
dollars.

133
00:09:04,741 --> 00:09:07,258
As n changes, the total changes with it.

134
00:09:08,399 --> 00:09:14,053
An algebraic expression combines numbers,
variables, and operations. Three x plus

135
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:15,589
five is an expression.

136
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:21,528
Its parts separated by plus or minus signs
are called terms. Here, the terms are

137
00:09:21,528 --> 00:09:22,695
three x and five.

138
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:28,329
The number multiplying a variable is its
coefficient, so three is the coefficient

139
00:09:28,329 --> 00:09:28,649
of x.

140
00:09:29,099 --> 00:09:32,427
A term with no variable, like five, is
called a constant.

141
00:09:32,566 --> 00:09:36,190
An expression is not the same as an
equation.

142
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:41,951
An equation has an equal sign and states
that two things are equal, like three x

143
00:09:41,951 --> 00:09:43,744
plus five equals seventeen.

144
00:09:44,194 --> 00:09:49,035
An expression is just a value we can
calculate. We simplify or evaluate

145
00:09:49,035 --> 00:09:51,490
expressions, and we solve equations.

146
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:57,667
To evaluate an expression, substitute the
value of the variable, then follow the

147
00:09:57,667 --> 00:09:58,926
order of operations.

148
00:09:59,376 --> 00:10:02,725
Let's evaluate three x plus five when x
equals four.

149
00:10:03,175 --> 00:10:06,141
Replace x with four: three times four,
plus five.

150
00:10:06,591 --> 00:10:10,111
Multiply first, to get twelve plus five,
which is seventeen.

151
00:10:11,233 --> 00:10:16,399
Now an expression with two variables: two
a squared, minus b, when a equals three

152
00:10:16,399 --> 00:10:17,547
and b equals five.

153
00:10:17,997 --> 00:10:20,835
Substitute: two times three squared, minus
five.

154
00:10:21,285 --> 00:10:25,551
Exponent first: three squared is nine.
Then two times nine is eighteen.

155
00:10:26,001 --> 00:10:27,943
And eighteen minus five is thirteen.

156
00:10:29,066 --> 00:10:31,775
We can also translate words into
expressions.

157
00:10:32,225 --> 00:10:37,490
Five more than twice a number. Let n be
the number. Twice the number is two n, and

158
00:10:37,490 --> 00:10:39,095
five more means add five.

159
00:10:39,545 --> 00:10:41,785
So the expression is two n plus five.

160
00:10:42,235 --> 00:10:47,552
Watch out for phrases like three less than
a number. That's n minus three, not three

161
00:10:47,552 --> 00:10:48,059
minus n.

162
00:10:49,199 --> 00:10:54,917
Your turn. Evaluate x squared, minus four
x, plus one, when x equals negative two.

163
00:10:55,367 --> 00:10:58,972
Pause the video and try it. Be careful
with the negative sign.

164
00:10:59,422 --> 00:11:04,931
Substitute, using parentheses: negative
two in parentheses, squared, minus four

165
00:11:04,931 --> 00:11:06,953
times negative two, plus one.

166
00:11:07,403 --> 00:11:12,603
Negative two squared is positive four.
Minus four times negative two is plus

167
00:11:12,603 --> 00:11:13,013
eight.

168
00:11:13,463 --> 00:11:16,450
So we get four plus eight plus one, which
is thirteen.

169
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:22,632
Here's a worked example on evaluating an
expression, with negative numbers to make

170
00:11:22,632 --> 00:11:23,552
it interesting.

171
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:30,582
Evaluate three a squared, minus two a b,
plus b, when a is negative two and b is

172
00:11:30,582 --> 00:11:30,931
five.

173
00:11:32,067 --> 00:11:36,975
Replace each variable with its value, and
always put the substituted numbers in

174
00:11:36,975 --> 00:11:37,720
parentheses.

175
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:42,408
Exponents first. Negative two squared is
positive four.

176
00:11:43,533 --> 00:11:49,127
Now multiply. Three times four is twelve.
Two times negative two times five is

177
00:11:49,127 --> 00:11:50,275
negative twenty.

178
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:54,984
Subtracting negative twenty is the same as
adding twenty.

179
00:11:56,133 --> 00:11:58,864
Twelve plus twenty plus five is thirty
seven.

180
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,608
So the expression equals thirty seven when
a is negative two and b is five.

181
00:12:05,733 --> 00:12:10,761
Watch out. Put every substituted value in
parentheses, so the exponent applies to

182
00:12:10,761 --> 00:12:15,603
the whole negative number. And remember
that subtracting a negative turns into

183
00:12:15,603 --> 00:12:16,037
adding.

184
00:12:17,167 --> 00:12:23,447
Your turn. Evaluate x squared minus five x
y plus two y, when x is negative three and

185
00:12:23,447 --> 00:12:26,255
y is four. Pause the video and try it.

186
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:36,412
Negative three squared is nine. Five times
negative three times four is negative

187
00:12:36,412 --> 00:12:42,093
sixty, so minus that is plus sixty. Two
times four is eight. Nine plus sixty plus

188
00:12:42,093 --> 00:12:43,707
eight is seventy seven.

189
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:48,993
Why can you add numbers in any order, but
not subtract them in any order?

190
00:12:49,443 --> 00:12:53,946
The answer comes from a handful of
properties that every number follows. In

191
00:12:53,946 --> 00:12:57,848
this lesson, we'll meet them, and see why
they make algebra work.

192
00:12:58,966 --> 00:13:02,636
First, the commutative property. Commute
means to move around.

193
00:13:03,086 --> 00:13:08,487
For addition, a plus b equals b plus a.
For example, three plus five and five plus

194
00:13:08,487 --> 00:13:09,870
three are both eight.

195
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:13,584
For multiplication, a times b equals b
times a.

196
00:13:14,034 --> 00:13:19,525
But subtraction is not commutative. Five
minus three is two, while three minus five

197
00:13:19,525 --> 00:13:20,583
is negative two.

198
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:24,580
Next, the associative property. It's about
grouping.

199
00:13:25,030 --> 00:13:30,428
When you add three numbers, it doesn't
matter which pair you add first. a plus b,

200
00:13:30,428 --> 00:13:32,560
plus c, equals a, plus b plus c.

201
00:13:33,010 --> 00:13:39,013
The same is true for multiplication. Two
times five, times seven, equals two, times

202
00:13:39,013 --> 00:13:41,544
five times seven. Both are seventy.

203
00:13:42,666 --> 00:13:46,656
The most important one in algebra is the
distributive property.

204
00:13:47,106 --> 00:13:52,984
a times the quantity b plus c equals a b
plus a c. The a gets multiplied by each

205
00:13:52,984 --> 00:13:55,042
term inside the parentheses.

206
00:13:55,492 --> 00:14:00,843
Think of a rectangle that's three wide,
and x plus four long. Its area is three x

207
00:14:00,843 --> 00:14:01,636
plus twelve.

208
00:14:02,086 --> 00:14:06,480
So three times the quantity x plus four
equals three x plus twelve.

209
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:11,120
The distributive property also makes
mental math easier.

210
00:14:11,570 --> 00:14:16,838
Seven times ninety eight is the same as
seven times the quantity one hundred minus

211
00:14:16,838 --> 00:14:17,095
two.

212
00:14:17,545 --> 00:14:21,428
That's seven hundred minus fourteen, which
is six hundred eighty six.

213
00:14:22,566 --> 00:14:24,529
Finally, identities and inverses.

214
00:14:24,979 --> 00:14:31,036
Adding zero leaves a number unchanged, so
zero is the additive identity. Multiplying

215
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:35,795
by one leaves it unchanged, so one is the
multiplicative identity.

216
00:14:36,245 --> 00:14:40,737
Every number has an opposite. a plus
negative a equals zero. That's the

217
00:14:40,737 --> 00:14:41,813
additive inverse.

218
00:14:42,263 --> 00:14:47,235
And every number except zero has a
reciprocal. a times one over a equals one.

219
00:14:47,235 --> 00:14:49,431
That's the multiplicative inverse.

220
00:14:50,566 --> 00:14:53,169
Your turn. Name the property shown in each
line.

221
00:14:53,619 --> 00:14:59,918
Four times the quantity x minus two equals
four x minus eight. Six plus negative six

222
00:14:59,918 --> 00:15:05,992
equals zero. And two times five, times
seven, equals two, times five times seven.

223
00:15:06,442 --> 00:15:07,914
Pause the video and decide.

224
00:15:08,364 --> 00:15:13,459
The first is the distributive property.
The second is the additive inverse. The

225
00:15:13,459 --> 00:15:16,812
third is the associative property of
multiplication.

226
00:15:17,933 --> 00:15:22,584
Let's use the properties of operations to
do a hard-looking problem in our heads.

227
00:15:24,033 --> 00:15:29,075
Evaluate twenty five times seventeen times
four, plus eight times ninety nine,

228
00:15:29,075 --> 00:15:30,433
without a calculator.

229
00:15:31,566 --> 00:15:36,589
The commutative property lets us swap the
order of the factors. Move the four next

230
00:15:36,589 --> 00:15:37,753
to the twenty five.

231
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:42,889
The associative property lets us group
twenty five and four first.

232
00:15:44,033 --> 00:15:49,287
Twenty five times four is one hundred, and
one hundred times seventeen is seventeen

233
00:15:49,287 --> 00:15:49,793
hundred.

234
00:15:50,933 --> 00:15:53,685
Now write ninety nine as one hundred minus
one.

235
00:15:54,833 --> 00:15:59,654
The distributive property gives eight
times one hundred, minus eight times one.

236
00:15:59,654 --> 00:16:04,658
That's eight hundred minus eight, so the
total is two thousand four hundred ninety

237
00:16:04,658 --> 00:16:04,902
two.

238
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:10,038
The answer is two thousand four hundred
ninety two, and we never needed a

239
00:16:10,038 --> 00:16:10,641
calculator.

240
00:16:11,766 --> 00:16:16,281
Watch out. The commutative and associative
properties work for addition and

241
00:16:16,281 --> 00:16:21,157
multiplication, but not for subtraction or
division. Look for friendly pairs that

242
00:16:21,157 --> 00:16:25,912
make ten, a hundred or a thousand. And
when you distribute, multiply every term

243
00:16:25,912 --> 00:16:27,297
inside the parentheses.

244
00:16:28,433 --> 00:16:34,176
Your turn. Evaluate five times forty three
times twenty, plus six times one hundred

245
00:16:34,176 --> 00:16:36,390
two. Pause the video and try it.

246
00:16:39,933 --> 00:16:45,849
Five times twenty is one hundred, so the
first part is forty three hundred. Six

247
00:16:45,849 --> 00:16:50,951
times one hundred two is six hundred plus
twelve, which is six hundred twelve. The

248
00:16:50,951 --> 00:16:53,626
total is four thousand nine hundred
twelve.

249
00:16:54,766 --> 00:16:57,326
Long expressions can often be made much
shorter.

250
00:16:57,776 --> 00:17:02,514
In this lesson, we'll learn to spot like
terms, and combine them to simplify an

251
00:17:02,514 --> 00:17:03,173
expression.

252
00:17:04,299 --> 00:17:08,673
Like terms have exactly the same variable
part, with the same exponents.

253
00:17:09,123 --> 00:17:14,527
Three x and five x are like terms. So are
two y squared and negative seven y

254
00:17:14,527 --> 00:17:15,096
squared.

255
00:17:15,546 --> 00:17:20,096
But three x and three x squared are not
like terms, because the exponents are

256
00:17:20,096 --> 00:17:20,687
different.

257
00:17:21,137 --> 00:17:25,885
And four y and four are not like terms
either, because one has a variable and the

258
00:17:25,885 --> 00:17:26,705
other doesn't.

259
00:17:27,833 --> 00:17:32,862
To combine like terms, add or subtract
their coefficients, and keep the variable

260
00:17:32,862 --> 00:17:33,742
part the same.

261
00:17:34,192 --> 00:17:36,347
Three x plus five x is eight x.

262
00:17:36,797 --> 00:17:41,930
This works because of the distributive
property: three x plus five x equals the

263
00:17:41,930 --> 00:17:45,309
quantity three plus five, times x, which
is eight x.

264
00:17:45,759 --> 00:17:50,295
Think of it like three apples plus five
apples. You get eight apples, not eight

265
00:17:50,295 --> 00:17:51,156
apples squared.

266
00:17:52,299 --> 00:17:56,651
Let's simplify seven a, plus two b, minus
three a, plus six b.

267
00:17:57,101 --> 00:18:01,965
First, group the like terms. Seven a minus
three a, and two b plus six b.

268
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:06,810
Seven a minus three a is four a. Two b
plus six b is eight b.

269
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:11,942
So the expression simplifies to four a
plus eight b. We can't combine those,

270
00:18:11,942 --> 00:18:13,852
because they're not like terms.

271
00:18:14,999 --> 00:18:17,175
Sometimes you need to distribute first.

272
00:18:17,625 --> 00:18:21,508
Simplify two times the quantity x plus
three, plus four x.

273
00:18:21,958 --> 00:18:25,051
Distribute the two: two x plus six, plus
four x.

274
00:18:25,501 --> 00:18:29,277
Now combine two x and four x, to get six x
plus six.

275
00:18:30,399 --> 00:18:33,471
Be careful with a minus sign in front of
parentheses.

276
00:18:33,921 --> 00:18:39,784
In five x minus the quantity two x minus
four, the minus sign applies to every term

277
00:18:39,784 --> 00:18:40,279
inside.

278
00:18:40,729 --> 00:18:46,487
It becomes five x minus two x plus four.
Notice the minus four turned into plus

279
00:18:46,487 --> 00:18:46,851
four.

280
00:18:47,301 --> 00:18:49,435
Combining, we get three x plus four.

281
00:18:50,566 --> 00:18:55,801
Your turn. Simplify three times the
quantity two y minus one, minus y, plus

282
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:56,219
seven.

283
00:18:56,669 --> 00:18:58,120
Pause the video and try it.

284
00:18:58,570 --> 00:19:02,581
Distribute the three: six y minus three,
minus y, plus seven.

285
00:19:03,031 --> 00:19:09,332
Combine the y terms: six y minus y is five
y. Combine the constants: negative three

286
00:19:09,332 --> 00:19:10,775
plus seven is four.

287
00:19:11,225 --> 00:19:13,102
The answer is five y plus four.

288
00:19:14,233 --> 00:19:19,280
Now a worked example that mixes the
distributive property with combining like

289
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:19,673
terms.

290
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:26,942
Simplify three times the quantity two x
minus five, minus two times the quantity

291
00:19:26,942 --> 00:19:29,206
four x minus one, plus seven x.

292
00:19:30,333 --> 00:19:35,917
Distribute the three: three times two x is
six x, and three times negative five is

293
00:19:35,917 --> 00:19:37,074
negative fifteen.

294
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:43,946
Now distribute negative two. Negative two
times four x is negative eight x, and

295
00:19:43,946 --> 00:19:47,437
negative two times negative one is
positive two.

296
00:19:48,566 --> 00:19:51,382
Group the x terms together and the
constants together.

297
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:58,395
Six minus eight plus seven is five, so we
get five x. Negative fifteen plus two is

298
00:19:58,395 --> 00:19:59,689
negative thirteen.

299
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:04,054
The simplified expression is five x minus
thirteen.

300
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:09,692
Watch out. The minus sign in front of the
two goes with it, so you distribute

301
00:20:09,692 --> 00:20:14,126
negative two. That is the most common
mistake here. Only combine like terms,

302
00:20:14,126 --> 00:20:18,677
with the same variable and exponent. And
you can always check by plugging in a

303
00:20:18,677 --> 00:20:20,602
simple number, like x equals one.

304
00:20:21,733 --> 00:20:26,783
Your turn. Simplify four times the
quantity three y plus two, minus five

305
00:20:26,783 --> 00:20:31,973
times the quantity y minus three, minus
two y. Pause the video and try it.

306
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:41,917
Distribute to get twelve y plus eight,
minus five y plus fifteen, minus two y.

307
00:20:41,917 --> 00:20:47,543
The y terms give five y, and the constants
give twenty three. So it's five y plus

308
00:20:47,543 --> 00:20:48,446
twenty three.

309
00:20:49,566 --> 00:20:54,399
Let's finish the unit with one realistic
problem that uses everything from Unit

310
00:20:54,399 --> 00:20:54,643
One.

311
00:20:56,066 --> 00:21:00,819
Two friends share a phone plan. Each pays
twenty five dollars a month, plus ten

312
00:21:00,819 --> 00:21:05,451
cents per text. Ana sends t texts. Ben
sends twenty fewer than three times as

313
00:21:05,451 --> 00:21:09,963
many as Ana. Write and simplify an
expression for their total monthly cost,

314
00:21:09,963 --> 00:21:13,453
then find the cost when Ana sends one
hundred fifty texts.

315
00:21:14,599 --> 00:21:20,389
First translate the words. Three times as
many as Ana is three t, and twenty fewer

316
00:21:20,389 --> 00:21:24,626
means minus twenty. So Ben sends three t
minus twenty texts.

317
00:21:25,766 --> 00:21:31,256
The total is two monthly fees, plus ten
cents times Ana's texts, plus ten cents

318
00:21:31,256 --> 00:21:32,507
times Ben's texts.

319
00:21:33,633 --> 00:21:39,147
Multiply two times twenty five to get
fifty, and distribute the ten cents: zero

320
00:21:39,147 --> 00:21:40,822
point three t minus two.

321
00:21:41,966 --> 00:21:48,261
Combine like terms. Zero point one t plus
zero point three t is zero point four t,

322
00:21:48,261 --> 00:21:50,947
and fifty minus two is forty eight.

323
00:21:52,066 --> 00:21:55,159
For part b, substitute one hundred fifty
for t.

324
00:21:56,299 --> 00:22:01,648
Zero point four times one hundred fifty is
sixty, and sixty plus forty eight is one

325
00:22:01,648 --> 00:22:02,550
hundred eight.

326
00:22:03,699 --> 00:22:08,917
So the total monthly cost is zero point
four t plus forty eight dollars, and when

327
00:22:08,917 --> 00:22:13,619
Ana sends one hundred fifty texts, the
bill is one hundred eight dollars.

328
00:22:14,766 --> 00:22:20,161
Watch out. Twenty fewer than three times t
is three t minus twenty, not twenty minus

329
00:22:20,161 --> 00:22:25,364
three t. Distribute the ten cents to both
terms. And check your work by computing

330
00:22:25,364 --> 00:22:26,777
the bill the long way.

331
00:22:27,899 --> 00:22:32,830
Your turn. A gym charges a forty dollar
sign up fee for each of two people, plus

332
00:22:32,830 --> 00:22:37,762
fifteen dollars per class. One person
takes c classes, and the other takes two c

333
00:22:37,762 --> 00:22:42,754
minus three. Write and simplify the total
cost, then find it when c is six. Pause

334
00:22:42,754 --> 00:22:44,049
the video and try it.

335
00:22:47,566 --> 00:22:54,284
Eighty plus fifteen c plus fifteen times
two c minus three simplifies to forty five

336
00:22:54,284 --> 00:22:59,933
c plus thirty five. When c is six, that's
two hundred seventy plus thirty five, or

337
00:22:59,933 --> 00:23:01,793
three hundred five dollars.

338
